  "details": "For the sounds its pretty much based on the system in 2020\n\nWhen you interact with certain things it makes that classic noise\n\n(Eg, pressing the search button, clicking on a friends profile or clicking on a world ect..)\n\nThe legacy menu, i have an idea on how it would work, it wouldn’t be a theme or reskin, it would be a separate ui that you can toggle, for example [If “using legacy menu”=true] it would only show the old menu and hide the 2.0 menu(or put it outside of render distance) and when that Legacy toggle is off then it puts the old menu out of bounds or hidden and shows the current menu\n\nThat way ya’ll don’t need to rearrange everything on the new menu as a theme, sure having 2 menus that do almost the same thing is a lil excessive but i’ve seen alot of people who really wants to use the old menu, BTW you dont need to replace the HUD for this, then again you could also make a beta branch that is up to date but uses the ui from 2020 or 2018\n\nThis is all in a way the same as the “simple menu” idea someone else mentioned",
